.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH SSGRID 1 2000-1月 "sfit_options" "sfit_options"
.SH NAME
sfit_options \- create the fitting configuration object of the S-system network inference
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIsfit_options(\fBnormalize\fR as string = "log2", 
\fBpseudo\fR as double = 1, 
\fBsparsity\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBmax_edges\fR as integer = 3, 
\fBmax_regulators\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBl1\fR as double = 0.01, 
\fBstability\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBsmooth\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBprior_penalty\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBprior_sign_penalty\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBprior_rank_boost\fR as double = 1, 
\fBprior\fR as <generic> PriorNetwork = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBde_pop\fR as integer = 40, 
\fBde_iters\fR as integer = 1200, 
\fBseed\fR as integer = 1234567, 
\fBparallel\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBverbose\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBrefine\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBfinal_time\fR as double = 0, 
\fBprecise\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 0);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
create the fitting configuration object of the S-system network inference
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBnormalize\fB \fR\- 
 the normalization method of the gene expression matrix, could be 
 \fBlog2\fR(default), \fBnone\fR, \fBrowzscore\fR or \fBquantile\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpseudo\fB \fR\- the pseudo count that used by the log2 normalization.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsparsity\fB \fR\- 
 the sparsity threshold of the net elasticity, the interaction with a smaller 
 \fB|g - h|\fR than this threshold will not be kept in the network topology.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_edges\fB \fR\- the max number of the regulators that could be kept for each target gene.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_regulators\fB \fR\- 
 the max number of the candidate regulators for each target gene, the prior 
 supported regulators are always included before the correlation based 
 preselection; zero means that all of the genes will be used as candidate.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBl1\fB \fR\- the L1 penalty weight of the kinetic orders.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstability\fB \fR\- the penalty weight of a positive self loop.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsmooth\fB \fR\- 
 the moving average window that used in the numerical differentiation, 
 it is required by the noisy pseudotime data; zero means no smoothing.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_penalty\fB \fR\- the soft penalty weight of the interactions that are not supported by the prior.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_sign_penalty\fB \fR\- the penalty weight of the direction conflict against the prior.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_rank_boost\fB \fR\- the ranking boost of the prior supported edges in the sparsification.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior\fB \fR\- the prior knowledge network object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBde_pop\fB \fR\- the population size of the differential evolution solver.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBde_iters\fB \fR\- the max iteration number of the differential evolution solver.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBseed\fB \fR\- the random seed.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBparallel\fB \fR\- run the per gene fitting in parallel or not?. 
.PP
.PP
\fBverbose\fB \fR\- print the fitting progress or not?. 
.PP
.PP
\fBrefine\fB \fR\- 
 refine the kinetic parameters by the trajectory fitting after the 
 decoupled slope fitting?
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfinal_time\fB \fR\- the final time of the simulation, zero means the end of the time axis.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprecise\fB \fR\- the integration step of the simulation.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- the number of the simulation sample points, zero means auto.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [FittingOptions](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.SGrid.GRN.FittingOptions) object
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let opts = sfit_options(sparsity = 0.01, max_edges = 6, smooth = 9);
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ssGrid
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
